Make HDF5's dimension-scale code safe on a corrupt DIMENSION_LIST / REFERENCE_LIST attribute.

H5DSiterate_scales (and the other functions in hl/src/H5DS.c that read one of these
attributes) allocate one `hvl_t` per dimension of the dataset with malloc and fill them
with H5Aread, then read buf[dim].len and dereference buf[dim].p. Two corrupt shapes of
the attribute break that (found by fuzzing a corrupt UGRID netCDF file through
nc_inq_var -> get_attached_info -> H5DSiterate_scales):

  * an attribute with fewer entries than the dataset has dimensions leaves the rest of
    the buffer unwritten, and the code loads a pointer from uninitialised memory (ASan's
    malloc fill shows as 0xbebebebebebebebe). malloc becomes calloc, so such an entry is
    empty (len 0, p NULL);
  * an entry the library read with a length but no data (p NULL) is then indexed by the
    loops that follow. Right after each of the five H5Aread calls into an `hvl_t` array
    an entry whose p is NULL is made empty (len 0).

Both are the existing "empty list" case, which the callers already handle; a valid file
never has either shape, so behaviour on valid files is unchanged. This is a local fix
for the instrumented fuzz build, not a backport, and it has not been reported upstream
(HDF5 1.14.6).

--- a/hl/src/H5DS.c
+++ b/hl/src/H5DS.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@
             goto out;
 
         /* allocate and initialize the VL */
-        buf = (hvl_t *)malloc((size_t)rank * sizeof(hvl_t));
+        buf = (hvl_t *)calloc((size_t)rank, sizeof(hvl_t));
         if (buf == NULL)
             goto out;
 
@@ -358,13 +358,17 @@
             goto out;
 
         /* allocate and initialize the VL */
-        buf = (hvl_t *)malloc((size_t)rank * sizeof(hvl_t));
+        buf = (hvl_t *)calloc((size_t)rank, sizeof(hvl_t));
         if (buf == NULL)
             goto out;
 
         /* read */
         if (H5Aread(aid, tid, buf) < 0)
             goto out;
+        /* a corrupt attribute can leave a length without data: make such an entry empty */
+        for (int rank_k = 0; rank_k < rank; rank_k++)
+            if (buf[rank_k].p == NULL)
+                buf[rank_k].len = 0;
 
         /* check to avoid inserting duplicates. it is not FAIL, just do nothing */
         /* iterate all the REFs in this dimension IDX */
@@ -841,13 +845,17 @@
